    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640">

                <pb facs="0769" n="1603" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1603"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.6131/14</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-03T10:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 3, 1918, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 4, 9.12 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2765. French military attaché informs me that under Helfferich’s leadership
                    Germans have founded a provisioning bureau in Constantinople which is organizing
                    purchase of wheat and other grain in Ukraine which is routed to Odessa and
                    Crimean ports. All barges obtainable, even in Holland, have been bought to carry
                    grain up the Danube.</p>
                <pb facs="0770" n="1604" xml:id="pg1604"/>
                <p>Bureau has representative in Berne and has offered grain to Switzerland in return
                    for her economic independence. Meeting of Federal Council held last night to
                    consider sending Swiss representative to Ukraine. Decision not known.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
